From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 04:54:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] kk: MESA_KK_DEBUG=memory logs the driver's live memory by
 kind

Red Dead Redemption 2's Story load ends at iOS's 8,192 MB per-process
limit, and the graphics ledger reaches 1.5 GB at its landing page while
host malloc grows by about 790 MB as the game creates the 3,136
pipelines of its 465 MB pipeline cache. Which part of that is the
game's device memory, which is the driver's own buffers, which is
Metal's (pipeline states), and which is the pipeline cache's data held
in host memory was not known.

With MESA_KK_DEBUG=memory, a queue submit logs one line at most every
10 s:

  [kk-mem] metal=MiB bos=MiB memory=N/MiB internal=N/MiB
    descriptor=N/MiB query=N/MiB command=N/MiB | shaders=N
    pipelines=N msl=MiB | cache raw=N/MiB precomp=N/MiB MiB

metal is MTLDevice.currentAllocatedSize. bos is the sum of the live
buffer objects KosmicKrisp allocated, split by what they back: device
memory (vkAllocateMemory, imported memory not counted), the driver's
own buffers, descriptor pools, query pools and tables, and command
buffer upload memory. shaders and pipelines count the live kk_shader
objects and those holding a Metal pipeline state; msl is the MSL source
they keep for serialization. raw and precomp are the pipeline cache
objects the Vulkan runtime holds in host memory: entries imported and
not yet used (raw data objects) and precompiled NIR shaders.

Without the flag nothing is counted or logged, except the buffer
object byte counts (two atomics per allocation and free).

Class: diagnostics
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-20-rdr2-kk-memory.md
Offered-upstream: no
